From: Thorch Android storage adaptation
Subject: [PATCH] Guard legacy HWKM eviction before initialization

UFS probe clears all keyslots before ICE/TME initialization. Qualcomm's
vendor HWKM implementation skips eviction until initialization is complete.
Avoid accessing clock-gated ICE registers or invoking legacy SCM at probe.

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/ice.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/ice.c
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/ice.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/ice.c
@@ -507,6 +507,12 @@
 int qcom_ice_evict_key(struct qcom_ice *ice, int slot)
 {
 	if (ice->android_legacy_hwkm) {
+		/* UFS clears every slot during probe, before ICE clocks and the
+		 * TME transport are ready. Match the vendor HWKM eviction guard:
+		 * no MMIO or secure-world clear before HWKM initialization.
+		 */
+		if (!ice->hwkm_init_complete)
+			return 0;
 		qcom_ice_writel(ice, 0, QCOM_ICE_REG_CRYPTOCFG(slot));
 		wmb();
 		return qcom_scm_legacy_ice_clear_key(slot * 2, 0);
